{There is great room for improvement noticeable in both players; but especially so in the Cantab. We illustrate the position [where Black's last move was 15...f6], when White misses the chance of gaining a piece:} 16. Qh5 $2 ({In playing} 16. f5 {he would have gained a piece.}) 16... f5 {However, he obtained a fair attack with} 17. Rf3 {, 18 Rg3, and the opening of the h-file. His opponent met this attack by coming out with his King and forcing the exchange of Queens on the 34th move; he gained a piece on the 40th move with an easy won position, which the Cantab prolonged until the 57th move, when he resigned. Sources: Chess-Monthly, Vol.5, May 1884, p275 (though the position given there must be wrong, with a R on a4. The position is correctly given in The Field, 12 April 1884)} 0-1

